# Downloading a binary response body instead of printing it -- printing
# raw image bytes to your terminal would just be garbage, so the "run"
# command's "-download" flag saves them to a file instead. See
# doc/usage.md's "-download" section.
#
# Run `make httpbin-up` first, then:
#
#   httpfly run -download photo.png 4_download.http
#
# (there's only one request in this file, so -name isn't required -- with
# more than one, -download would require it to pick which response to save)

###
# @name GetPNG
GET http://localhost:8080/image/png HTTP/1.1
Accept: image/png
